[{"category":"section","location":"","page":"Home","text":"<div id=\"landing\" class=\"landing\">\n<header class=\"landing-hero\">\n  <div class=\"landing-hero__text\">\n    <p class=\"landing-name\">CausalGraphs.jl</p>\n    <h1 class=\"landing-title\">A Julia-native framework for representing, analyzing, composing, comparing, and visualizing cause-effect knowledge and models.</h1>\n    <p class=\"landing-tagline\">Domain-independent causal relationships.</p>\n    <div class=\"landing-actions\">\n<a class=\"landing-btn landing-btn--brand\" href=\"./\">Get Started</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</header>\n<section class=\"landing-features\" aria-label=\"Features\">\n  <div class=\"landing-feature\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">🧠</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Cause-Effect Knowledge</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">Build structured graphs independent from models and views.</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"landing-feature\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">📦</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Multiple Models</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">Derive models from a single knowledge base without duplication.</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"landing-feature\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">🔬</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Metrology Support</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">First-class integration with uncertainty propagation workflows.</p>\n  </div>\n</section>\n</div>","title":"Home"},{"category":"section","location":"#API-Reference","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"#CausalGraphs.IshikawaLayout","page":"Home","text":"IshikawaLayout\n\nA structural layout representing an Ishikawa (Fishbone) diagram. Stores the main effect, category branches, and the underlying root causes for each category.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CausalGraphs.IshikawaLayout"},{"category":"method","location":"#CausalGraphs.to_dot-Tuple{Union{AbstractModel, CauseEffectGraph}}","page":"Home","text":"to_dot(g)\n\nGenerates a GraphViz DOT string representation of the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CausalGraphs.to_dot"}]
